# openOODA MCP Server — Editor Setup

File: ooda/mcp/docs/MCP_SETUP.oot

The openOODA MCP (Model Context Protocol) server is a pure-`.oo` self-hosted MCP server. It speaks MCP 3.0 over stdio (JSON-RPC 2.0 framed) and provides tools/list, tools/call, resources/list, resources/read, and a heartbeat health probe.

## How to launch

```sh
# stdio (the real editor case)
ooda mcp

# one-shot file mode
ooda mcp path/to/request.txt
```

## Capabilities

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `initialize` | Lifecycle start, server capabilities |
| `tools/list` | Enumerate the 23 typed tools |
| `tools/call` | Dispatch to a single tool, wrap the result |
| `resources/list` | Enumerate the 6 knowledge resources |
| `resources/read` | Read a specific resource (board, codex, schema, format, context-budget) |
| `ping` | Heartbeat (returns 7 server-wide health fields) |

## See also

- `protocol.oot` — the JSON-RPC 2.0 wire protocol
- `client_config.oot` — how to configure MCP clients
